#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<personname><firstname>Ben</firstname><surname>Burton</surname></"
"personname> <email>bab@debian.org</email>"
msgstr ""
"<व्यक्तिनाम><प्रथमनाम>बेन्</firstname><surname>बर्टन</surname></personname> "
"<email>bab@debian.org</email>"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:10
#. Tag: date
#, no-c-format
msgid "2003-04-07"
msgstr "२००३-०४-०७ ई"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:15
#. Tag: manvolnum
#, no-c-format
msgid "<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>"
msgstr "<मन्वोल्नुम्>१</मन्वोल्नुम्>"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:20
#. Tag: refpurpose
#, no-c-format
msgid "Extract message strings from UI and GUI-RC files"
msgstr "UI तथा GUI-RC सञ्चिकाभ्यः सन्देशस्ट्रिंग् निष्कासयन्तु"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:24
#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>extractrc</command> "
"<group><option><replaceable>filename</replaceable></option></group>"
msgstr ""
"<command>extractrc</command><group><option><replaceable> "
"सञ्चिकानाम</replaceable></option></group>"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:32
#. Tag: title
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "वर्णनम्‌"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:34
#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>extractrc</command> finds all text tags and other message strings "
"in the given files and writes the corresponding i18n() calls to standard "
"output so that xgettext can parse them."
msgstr ""
"<command>extractrc</command> दत्तसञ्चिकासु सर्वाणि पाठटैग्स् "
"अन्यसन्देशताराः च अन्विष्य तत्सम्बद्धानि i18n() आह्वानं मानकनिर्गमं प्रति "
"लिखति येन xgettext तान् विश्लेषणं कर्तुं शक्नोति"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:38
#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It understands both (&Qt;/&kde;) <application>designer</application>'s "
"<acronym>UI</acronym> files and &XML; GUI-RC files."
msgstr ""
"एतत् (&Qt;/&kde;) <application>designer</application> इत्यस्य "
"<acronym>UI</acronym> सञ्चिकाः &XML; GUI-RC सञ्चिकाः ।"

#: man-extractrc.1.docbook:42
#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid "This utility is part of the KDE Software Development Kit."
msgstr "इयं उपयोगिता KDE Software Development Kit इत्यस्य भागः अस्ति ।"
